From aaf23cb65359ef61a88a21ba0b50f189e08c4778 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ESP32S3VM gdma <gdma@esp32s3vm.invalid>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:41:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] hw/dma/esp_gdma: bounded descriptor walking, persistent
 cursors, handshake hooks

Rework the generic GDMA engine per docs/plans/peripherals-electrical.md
CORE-04 and TRM chapter 3 (GDMA Controller):

- Descriptor checks per TRM 3.4.6: owner bit (GDMA_x_CHECK_OWNER), DW1
  buffer window (internal 0x3FC88000-0x3FCFFFFF / external 0x3C000000-
  0x3DFFFFFF), DW2 next-descriptor window (internal RAM, 0 = end of
  list), and inlink burst alignment (TRM tables 3.4-2/3.4-3: word
  alignment for internal-RAM descriptors, block alignment per
  GDMA_IN_EXT_MEM_BK_SIZE for external-RAM descriptors; the internal
  window lies numerically above the external base so the window test
  must be explicit). Failures raise DSCR_ERR and halt the channel
  instead of looping or asserting on the host.
- Persistent descriptor + byte cursors per channel/direction: peripheral
  pumps (esp_gdma_read_channel/esp_gdma_write_channel) and memory-to-
  memory slices continue exactly where they stopped instead of
  restarting from the link address.
- Bounded work quantum (256 descriptor fetches per scheduled slice): a
  still-running chain stays armed (LINK.PARK reads 0) and continues
  through a main-loop bottom half, so valid streaming rings yield at
  quantum boundaries and the main loop (QMP/vCPU/chardev) is never
  starved, with either a stopped or a running virtual clock.
  Non-progressing cycles (16 fetches without moving a byte) raise
  DSCR_ERR; walk bounds are per slice / per pump call / per restart,
  never cumulative over the life of a chain.
- GDMA_xLINK semantics: PARK computed from the FSM state (reset value
  1), INLINK AUTO_RET reset value 1, START/RESTART/STOP self-clearing,
  STOP parks while keeping cursors for a later RESTART. RESTART follows
  TRM 3.4.5 (re-read DW2 of the last processed descriptor at DSCR_BF0),
  or resumes the byte cursor when a walk stopped mid-descriptor.
- CONF0 RST 1->0 resets the channel FSM and cursors (not only the FIFO);
  a descriptor error halts until reset or fresh START per TRM 3.4.6.
- GDMA_PERI_SEL stored as the 6-bit register field; S3 subclass
  validation hooks into esp_gdma_get_channel_periph, which now matches
  the peripheral selection AND the armed channel and never consumes
  another peripheral's channel.
- OUT EOF descriptor registers (GDMA_OUT_EOF_DES_ADDR / EOF_BFR_DES_ADDR)
  and IN_SUC_EOF_DES_ADDR maintained per TRM 3.5; memory-to-memory
  completion raises OUT_TOTAL_EOF only when the list actually ends.
- Receive descriptor writeback clears owner unconditionally and records
  the received length; suc_eof set by hardware on EOF-flagged data.
